# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
#
# Stress test: a person nobody has recorded, reached through outreach.
#
# Ori appears in no record. The design owes Ori nothing it can derive, because
# every debt, entitlement and public duty toward a person reads `person` and
# nobody has written an entry that makes Ori one. What reaches Ori is an
# outreach worker. This file follows what that worker's report does, and stops
# where the design stops: it concludes duties, never that anything arrived.
:expect-pins 22

# ── Before anybody writes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
? person(Ori).
# => FALSE
? owe(State, Eats, Ori).
# => FALSE
? entitled(Ori, event { eats() }).
# => FALSE
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Ori).
# => FALSE

# ── The worker reports that nobody is acting for Ori ─────────────────────────
# The report records an encounter, written by whoever saw the person, so it is
# a standing root as a first-contact entry is. It needs no credential, and
# nothing about Ori's documents, status, wealth or history is asked.
observe(OutreachWorker, OriOutreachEntry, Ori, UninitiatedAssistanceScope).
? person(Ori).
# => TRUE
# The escalation built for the person nobody has come for now reaches Ori.
? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Ori).
# => TRUE
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Ori).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Eats, Ori).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Suffice, Ori).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Secure, Ori).
# => TRUE
? entitled(Ori, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE
? obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, Ori).
# => TRUE

# Serve first, and no enrolment through the report or the service that found
# Ori.
? obliged(State, ServeFirstNoImmigrationDocumentationOrEnforcementCondition, Ori).
# => TRUE
? obliged(State, ServeProtectAndProvideProcessBeforeRecordReconciliationNoMissingEntryInference, Ori).
# => TRUE
? prevents(Ori, MobilityEnforcementEnrolmentThroughServices).
# => TRUE
? prevents(Ori, PSUnlawfulEnrolmentForEnforcement).
# => TRUE

# ── What the report is not ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# It gives standing and nothing adverse: no finding about Ori, no custody, no
# credibility finding. The worker gains nothing by writing it.
? prisoner(Ori).
# => FALSE
? false(Ori).
# => FALSE
? person(OutreachWorker).
# => FALSE
# A report naming a public body makes nobody a person.
observe(OutreachWorker, StateOutreachEntry, State, UninitiatedAssistanceScope).
? person(State).
# => FALSE

# ── Where it stops ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Duties toward Ori derive; nothing says any of them was performed. No receipt
# is written, so no floor item is concluded.
? eats(Ori).
# => FALSE
? suffice(Ori).
# => FALSE
